    "title": "Our Family of Planets",
    "subtitle": "Eight planets, but not one of them is the same.",
    "body": "Eight planets travel around the Sun. They make one big family. But the planets are not the same at all.\n\nLook at where they sit. Four small planets stay <u>near</u> the Sun. Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars are close and warm. The other four are far and cold.\n\nNow look at what they are made of. The close planets have hard ground. You could stand on this rocky land. The far planets are big balls of gas. They have <mark>no solid ground</mark> to stand on.\n\nThe order matters too. Mercury comes first, and we count out to Neptune. Earth is third in this line.\n\nSo each planet has its own spot. Together they are our family of planets.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/06.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Eight planets in a line — small rocky ones near the Sun, big gas ones far away."
  },
